01:00:56,619 --> 01:00:58,394
we will work with what we have.

995
01:01:00,757 --> 01:01:03,246
So, I've come up with a routine
that we can do with a small crew.

996
01:01:03,326 --> 01:01:05,748
Wait, wait. I create the routines.

997
01:01:05,828 --> 01:01:06,863
- Come on! Don't be such a...
- I...

998
01:01:07,630 --> 01:01:09,268
Be careful what you say.

999
01:01:09,899 --> 01:01:13,346
Okay. You're starting to sound
a lot like the old Destiny.

1000
01:01:14,070 --> 01:01:16,426
Well, if you like the new Destiny so much,

1001
01:01:16,506 --> 01:01:17,961
why don't you go join her?

1002
01:01:18,041 --> 01:01:20,521
Because I don't have room
for people who doubt me.

1003
01:01:21,344 --> 01:01:25,835
Wow. Was I an idiot, falling for your crap.

1004
01:01:25,915 --> 01:01:27,223
I'm out.

1005
01:01:33,890 --> 01:01:36,530
Any other losers who want to join her?

1006
01:01:39,429 --> 01:01:41,272
I didn't think so.

1007
01:01:46,402 --> 01:01:48,040
- That was hot.
- What was hot?

1008
01:01:48,404 --> 01:01:49,508
You playing like Cruella de Vil.

1009
01:01:50,940 --> 01:01:53,045
- I wasn't playing.
- Okay.

1010
01:01:53,843 --> 01:01:56,483
Okay, from now on no one's in charge.

1011
01:01:57,013 --> 01:01:59,168
Everybody's opinions are welcome.

1012
01:01:59,248 --> 01:02:01,571
Because it was exhausting
being a boss-ass bitch.

1013
01:02:02,952 --> 01:02:05,375
Okay, we need to reach out to anyone
we can to be a part of our squad.

1014
01:02:05,455 --> 01:02:07,610
We only have four more weeks
to prepare for the Cheer Challenge.

1015
01:02:07,690 --> 01:02:08,964
Okay.

1016
01:02:12,962 --> 01:02:15,585
What are you doing here?
Hannah send you to spy on us?

1017
01:02:15,665 --> 01:02:17,620
I'm here for the same reason you're here.

1018
01:02:17,700 --> 01:02:20,723
To win the Cheer Challenge
with my cheer family.

1019
01:02:20,803 --> 01:02:22,725
I know things haven't been smooth between us

1020
01:02:22,805 --> 01:02:24,113
and that's on me.

1021
01:02:24,440 --> 01:02:27,512
But I want you to know
I really do appreciate you.

1022
01:02:49,699 --> 01:02:51,645
Yeah, guys. That was awesome.

1023
01:02:59,008 --> 01:03:00,487
Let's go again.

1024
01:03:03,346 --> 01:03:04,484
Over here.

1025
01:03:13,523 --> 01:03:16,479
Ew. Gross. They're all booed up.

1026
01:03:16,559 --> 01:03:17,780
There's no accounting for taste,

1027
01:03:17,860 --> 01:03:19,066
and I'm talking about Didit's.

1028
01:03:22,365 --> 01:03:24,038
They look so pathetic.

1029
01:03:24,500 --> 01:03:25,955
And without you guys, they're done.

1030
01:03:26,035 --> 01:03:27,023
Who cares?

1031
01:03:27,103 --> 01:03:30,560
Well, not me, but I thought you were gonna
ask the other guys to join our squad.

1032
01:03:30,640 --> 01:03:32,642
I tried, but they ain't feeling it.

1033
01:03:33,209 --> 01:03:36,452
Besides, why would you want
the rest when you've got the best.

1034
01:03:36,579 --> 01:03:39,135
Did you just try to cheersuade me?

1035
01:03:39,215 --> 01:03:40,203
Sure did.

1036
01:03:40,283 --> 01:03:41,728
Don't do that.

1037
01:03:47,557 --> 01:03:49,212
That was a good practice, right?

1038
01:03:49,292 --> 01:03:50,880
I'm telling you, we can still do this.

1039
01:03:50,960 --> 01:03:52,098
Yeah, right.

1040
01:03:52,461 --> 01:03:54,964
Hey! You're cheerleaders. Cheer the hell up.

1041
01:03:55,364 --> 01:03:56,604
Don't worry. They'll come around.

1042
01:03:57,366 --> 01:03:59,155
I mean, the choreography
was still good though, right?

1043
01:03:59,235 --> 01:04:00,556
- Yeah.
- And the routine was...

1044
01:04:00,636 --> 01:04:01,691
- Great.
- And the stunts were...

1045
01:04:01,771 --> 01:04:02,759
- On point.
- Exactly.

1046
01:04:02,839 --> 01:04:04,560
So, why do I feel like we're missing...

1047
01:04:04,640 --> 01:04:06,662
Balls. Literally and figuratively.

1048
01:04:06,742 --> 01:04:07,797
We still have some of our boys.

1049
01:04:07,877 --> 01:04:09,447
No, I think she was talking about Jeff's.

1050
01:04:09,579 --> 01:04:10,600
Oh. Ew!

1051
01:04:10,680 --> 01:04:13,302
No, not just Jeff. The rest of the guys, too.

1052
01:04:13,382 --> 01:04:15,204
I mean, they were
throwing down some mad flavor.

1053
01:04:15,284 --> 01:04:16,405
"Mad flavor"?

1054
01:04:16,485 --> 01:04:17,673
Oh, my God. She's starting to sound like him.

1055
01:04:17,753 --> 01:04:20,276
- Yeah.
- So what are we gonna do?

1056
01:04:20,356 --> 01:04:23,646
Well, my femtuition is telling me

1057
01:04:23,726 --> 01:04:25,782
we need to suck it up
and figure how to get the boys back.

1058
01:04:25,862 --> 01:04:27,784
Yeah, but Hannah has
her claws into half of them

1059
01:04:27,864 --> 01:04:30,853
and the other half we have tried every
means of messaging with no response.

1060
01:04:30,933 --> 01:04:32,321
We're starting to sound desperate.

1061
01:04:32,401 --> 01:04:34,074
I don't know what else to do.

1062
01:04:35,972 --> 01:04:38,646
But I think I know who might.

1063
01:04:41,377 --> 01:04:44,586
Ah. Okay, you really need to know
how to finish a conversation.

1064
01:04:51,487 --> 01:04:53,609
Now why didn't I know about this place?

1065
01:04:53,689 --> 01:04:56,602
Not a lot of people do.
You kind of have to know somebody.

1066
01:05:00,696 --> 01:05:02,266
So, is your work in here?

1067
01:05:02,832 --> 01:05:05,955
No. These pieces are done
by the kings of graffiti art.

1068
01:05:06,035 --> 01:05:07,190
You have to earn it.

1069
01:05:07,270 --> 01:05:09,682
Well, I think your work is great.

1070
01:05:20,549 --> 01:05:23,928
Okay, what's up?
There's something you're not telling me.

1071
01:05:25,354 --> 01:05:27,844
You must have heard I drove
some of your boys away.

1072
01:05:27,924 --> 01:05:30,780
You called them ghetto.
And not in a good way.

1073
01:05:30,860 --> 01:05:32,748
I know. I know I should have never said that

1074
01:05:32,828 --> 01:05:34,383
even if I thought no one was gonna hear it.

1075
01:05:34,463 --> 01:05:37,153
This is why I don't deal
with social media and all that crap.

1076
01:05:37,233 --> 01:05:38,769
Okay. Can you just help me get the guys back?

1077
01:05:39,168 --> 01:05:40,389
I'm staying out of it.

1078
01:05:40,469 --> 01:05:41,724
Just tell me what I need to do.

1079
01:05:41,804 --> 01:05:43,593
All you have to do is be straight with them.

1080
01:05:43,673 --> 01:05:45,761
How am I supposed to do that
when they won't even talk to me?

1081
01:05:45,841 --> 01:05:47,897
- They're giving you the silent treatment.
- Yes.

1082
01:05:47,977 --> 01:05:50,566
Wait. You physically walked up to them,

1083
01:05:50,646 --> 01:05:52,956
said something, and they wouldn't respond?

1084
01:05:54,317 --> 01:05:56,797
Oh. You mean, like, in person?

1085
01:05:58,354 --> 01:06:00,643
No. No, I haven't done that yet.

1086
01:06:00,723 --> 01:06:03,101
That's why I'm not an Internet slave.

1087
01:06:03,292 --> 01:06:05,781
I am not a slave to the Internet.

1088
01:06:05,861 --> 01:06:08,084
Oh. Well, prove it. Give me your phone.

1089
01:06:08,164 --> 01:06:09,418
Why? What are you gonna do with it?

1090
01:06:09,498 --> 01:06:11,535
I'm gonna turn it off and hold
onto it for the rest of our date.

1091
01:06:11,867 --> 01:06:13,489
Well, what if there's a cheermergency?

1092
01:06:13,569 --> 01:06:15,071
Globally or just in the city?

1093
01:06:16,138 --> 01:06:18,414
Fine.

1094
01:06:19,275 --> 01:06:20,345
Thank you.

1095
01:06:23,579 --> 01:06:24,614
Okay, now what?

1096
01:06:25,247 --> 01:06:26,702
I don't know.

1097
01:06:26,782 --> 01:06:29,353
Maybe notice anything bigger
than a five-inch screen?

1098
01:06:32,021 --> 01:06:33,295
God! You're like 100.

1099
01:06:58,814 --> 01:07:00,002
What are you doing?

1100
01:07:00,082 --> 01:07:01,925
We're not leaving until
you come back to the squad.

1101
01:07:05,588 --> 01:07:08,477
Well, that's gonna be awkward
'cause we're just about to leave.

1102
01:07:08,557 --> 01:07:11,766
Besides, we weren't planning
to come back to your squad...

1103
01:07:12,261 --> 01:07:14,717
It's about a quarter to never.

1104
01:07:14,797 --> 01:07:16,152
What are you, like, two?

1105
01:07:16,232 --> 01:07:18,521
Look, I don't mind when you're mean
to me 'cause I know you like me.

1106
01:07:18,601 --> 01:07:21,411
- What?
- Destiny, that diary business was foul.

1107
01:07:22,071 --> 01:07:23,659
- And everybody saw it.
- I know.

1108
01:07:23,739 --> 01:07:26,662
And I'm sorry. And this is
fempossible for me to admit,

1109
01:07:26,742 --> 01:07:29,313
but we haven't been the same
since you guys left.

1110
01:07:29,745 --> 01:07:31,500
Oh. Why not?

1111
01:07:31,580 --> 01:07:34,026
'Cause all you ever did was try
and change everything about us.

1112
01:07:34,183 --> 01:07:36,772
I mean, our energy, our style. My jokes.

1113
01:07:36,852 --> 01:07:39,298
Okay, your jokes were weak.
Let's not call that a loss.

1114
01:07:40,956 --> 01:07:42,244
Okay, I'll give you that.

1115
01:07:42,324 --> 01:07:45,614
Look, when we joined up with you, we thought
it was because we'd actually add something.

1116
01:07:45,694 --> 01:07:47,674
And you weren't just gonna use us for muscle.

1117
01:07:47,963 --> 01:07:50,619
- Oh, wow. Did we reverse sexism them?
- I believe we did.

1118
01:07:50,699 --> 01:07:51,871
That wasn't our intention.

1119
01:07:54,103 --> 01:07:56,025
Okay. Yeah, maybe it was,

1120
01:07:56,105 --> 01:07:59,028
but we get that you brought
more than we realized.

1121
01:07:59,108 --> 01:08:00,730
Yeah, you should have thought about that

1122
01:08:00,810 --> 01:08:02,687
before you cheermiliated us and...

1123
01:08:03,079 --> 01:08:05,434
I can't believe I just said that.

1124
01:08:05,514 --> 01:08:06,857
That's because cheer is in your blood now.

1125
01:08:07,783 --> 01:08:10,106
Okay, look. I can't speak
for the rest of the guys,

1126
01:08:10,186 --> 01:08:13,690
but just give me one good reason
why I should cheer with you.

1127
01:08:14,256 --> 01:08:15,326
'Cause I am.

1128
01:08:18,694 --> 01:08:20,833
- What?
- You heard me. I'm in.

1129
01:08:21,430 --> 01:08:23,486
Are you serious? Why?

1130
01:08:23,566 --> 01:08:26,155
I really dig that you love
spending time in my world.

1131
01:08:26,235 --> 01:08:28,324
I figured I should maybe spend
some time in yours.

1132
01:08:28,404 --> 01:08:30,816
Besides, I love a challenge.

1133
01:08:34,176 --> 01:08:35,450
What do you say?

1134
01:08:36,946 --> 01:08:37,947
Let's do it!

1135
01:08:40,916 --> 01:08:42,471
All right, I guess we're back in.

1136
01:08:42,551 --> 01:08:44,224
Yes! Then let's practice.

1137
01:08:44,587 --> 01:08:45,574
Or we don't have to practice.

1138
01:08:45,654 --> 01:08:47,476
We can chill or hang out
or do whatever you want.

1139
01:08:47,556 --> 01:08:49,512
No, no, no. We only got
two weeks to get ready. So...

1140
01:08:49,592 --> 01:08:50,646
Yeah, I could cheer.

1141
01:08:50,726 --> 01:08:53,297
- Yeah.
- Okay. Then let's do this.

1142
01:10:35,531 --> 01:10:37,720
Thank you for taking
the time to talk to me, Destiny.

1143
01:10:37,800 --> 01:10:38,821
Thank you for having me.

1144
01:10:38,901 --> 01:10:39,889
I wanted to chat with you

1145
01:10:39,969 --> 01:10:43,325
because this whole worldwide cheer smackdown,

1146
01:10:43,405 --> 01:10:44,475
it started with you.

1147
01:10:45,107 --> 01:10:47,530
Yeah. I'm not proud of it though.

1148
01:10:47,610 --> 01:10:50,099
It took my team turning on me
to get my attention.

1149
01:10:50,179 --> 01:10:54,069
How about I remind everybody
that those masked cheerleaders

1150
01:10:54,149 --> 01:10:57,289
calling themselves The Truth
are actually your former teammates.

1151
01:10:57,953 --> 01:10:59,408
Yeah. Some of them.

1152
01:10:59,488 --> 01:11:01,764
It's true. And totally embarrassing.

1153
01:11:02,258 --> 01:11:03,646
I bet.

1154
01:11:03,726 --> 01:11:07,449
Here you were thinking that they
were your friends and cheer mates.

1155
01:11:07,529 --> 01:11:08,530
Now that's rude.

1156
01:11:08,864 --> 01:11:11,708
I don't blame them, though.
I was out of control.

1157
01:11:12,301 --> 01:11:13,489
Why do you say that?

1158
01:11:13,569 --> 01:11:16,072
I was so caught up
in this whole cheerlebrity thing.

1159
01:11:16,939 --> 01:11:19,715
Life's not about how many likes
or followers you have.

1160
01:11:20,276 --> 01:11:23,966
It's about how many friends
are willing to stand by you,

1161
01:11:24,046 --> 01:11:26,219
beside you. Catch you in a cradle.

1162
01:11:28,317 --> 01:11:31,355
Because a squad is nothing unless
you have each other's backs.

1163
01:11:31,854 --> 01:11:35,211
I was trying to be someone on social media.

1164
01:11:35,291 --> 01:11:36,793
I forgot who I really was.

1165
01:11:37,459 --> 01:11:38,681
Now that's deep.

1166
01:11:38,761 --> 01:11:43,152
Anywho, the whole world will be
watching and voting tomorrow.

1167
01:11:43,232 --> 01:11:44,587
Tell them why they should vote for you.

1168
01:11:44,667 --> 01:11:46,488
No. Don't vote for me.

1169
01:11:46,568 --> 01:11:47,590
What?

1170
01:11:47,670 --> 01:11:50,893
Vote for the Rebels because
now we're all in this together.

1171
01:11:50,973 --> 01:11:54,463
Thank you, Destiny. Best of luck tomorrow.

1172
01:11:54,543 --> 01:11:56,113
No, thank you, Cheer Goddess.

1173
01:12:00,349 --> 01:12:01,837
How do you think I did?

1174
01:12:01,917 --> 01:12:03,072
You got way more likes...

1175
01:12:03,152 --> 01:12:05,996
No, not that. I'm asking what you thought.

1176
01:12:06,088 --> 01:12:07,328
Oh.

1177
01:12:07,589 --> 01:12:09,227
You were the Destiny I've always liked.

1178
01:12:10,959 --> 01:12:12,563
Well, that's the only like that matters.

1179
01:12:29,044 --> 01:12:32,787
So, what do you think? And be nice.
This was my first one.

1180
01:12:36,485 --> 01:12:38,192
It's you.

1181
01:12:48,163 --> 01:12:50,586
Tell me why again we're at this
disgusting old warehouse

1182
01:12:50,666 --> 01:12:52,054
in the middle of nowhere to do our routine

1183
01:12:52,134 --> 01:12:53,622
when we have a state-of-the-art gym?

1184
01:12:53,702 --> 01:12:55,090
Well, the Cheer Goddess agreed with The Truth

1185
01:12:55,170 --> 01:12:57,059
that the Rebels gym gives us
a home advantage.

1186
01:12:57,139 --> 01:12:59,328
It screams three times national champions.

1187
01:12:59,408 --> 01:13:01,230
This place is anonymous.

1188
01:13:01,310 --> 01:13:03,290
Yeah, and for good reason.

1189
01:13:12,421 --> 01:13:13,422
Hey, Destiny.

1190
01:13:14,089 --> 01:13:17,502
After we're done here, you're gonna
realize your cheers are so old

1191
01:13:17,926 --> 01:13:19,803
you're gonna need a landline to dial them in.

1192
01:13:20,596 --> 01:13:21,717
Isn't that right, Didit?

1193
01:13:21,797 --> 01:13:23,786
Yeah. What's up, Jeff?

1194
01:13:23,866 --> 01:13:24,953
Yo, what's up, man?

1195
01:13:25,033 --> 01:13:26,088
What are you doing?

1196
01:13:26,168 --> 01:13:27,156
I'm showing my man some love.

1197
01:13:27,236 --> 01:13:28,943
- We're still boys.
- Yeah.

1198
01:13:29,938 --> 01:13:32,161
No, no, no. Wait, wait, wait. No!
No, no, no, no.

1199
01:13:32,241 --> 01:13:34,930
We hate them right now.
There is no love at a smackdown.

1200
01:13:35,010 --> 01:13:38,367
You, you, you. You. All of you.

1201
01:13:38,447 --> 01:13:39,619
You're all going down.

1202
01:13:40,849 --> 01:13:43,125
You know, there's a better way
you could have said that.

1203
01:13:43,786 --> 01:13:45,129
You could have said...

1204
01:13:45,921 --> 01:13:46,922
Bring it!

1205
01:13:57,499 --> 01:14:00,589
Good evening and welcome to the smackdown.

1206
01:14:00,669 --> 01:14:03,081
I'm your host, the Cheer Goddess.

1207
01:14:03,639 --> 01:14:05,928
The rules of the smackdown are simple.

1208
01:14:06,008 --> 01:14:07,229
There are no rules.

1209
01:14:07,309 --> 01:14:10,065
Teams can use any combination of lifts,

1210
01:14:10,145 --> 01:14:12,201
floor work and dance choreography.

1211
01:14:12,281 --> 01:14:15,871
Over 20 teams are competing
from more than 12 countries.

1212
01:14:15,951 --> 01:14:19,108
So remember, the world
is watching and voting.

1213
01:14:19,188 --> 01:14:21,910
So cheer your hearts out,
my little cheer minions.

1214
01:14:21,990 --> 01:14:23,094
And let's begin.

1215
01:14:23,392 --> 01:14:26,464
Cheer world, it's time to break the Internet.

1216
01:14:26,562 --> 01:14:30,135
Let's hear it for the Costa Rica
All Star Twisters.

1217
01:15:06,335 --> 01:15:08,576
What a tasty piece of spirit candy.

1218
01:15:08,937 --> 01:15:12,077
Let's give it up for the ViQueens of Norway.

1219
01:15:55,617 --> 01:15:57,961
Now let's see how they get down down under.

1220
01:15:58,186 --> 01:16:00,826
Starlets, Team Orion from Australia.

1221
01:16:32,754 --> 01:16:34,131
Hey. Are you nervous?

1222
01:16:35,157 --> 01:16:38,001
Cheerleaders don't get nervous. We get ready.

1223
01:16:38,660 --> 01:16:40,264
Oh. Good.

1224
01:16:41,129 --> 01:16:42,267
But I'm nervous.

1225
01:16:45,334 --> 01:16:48,824
Next up, Cheer XS from France.

1226
01:17:09,658 --> 01:17:12,798
Unity All Stars Block
from the United Kingdom.

1227
01:17:30,212 --> 01:17:32,749
Please welcome the Berlin Titans.

1228
01:17:46,862 --> 01:17:49,536
Nova All Stars from Singapore.

1229
01:18:05,781 --> 01:18:08,403
FYI, cheer family, the hits from

1230
01:18:08,483 --> 01:18:11,173
the cheer smackdown are insane.

1231
01:18:11,253 --> 01:18:13,308
We are trending around the globe,

1232
01:18:13,388 --> 01:18:16,979
with the hashtags cheersmackdown
and bring it on.

1233
01:18:17,059 --> 01:18:18,847
So let's keep that momentum going

1234
01:18:18,927 --> 01:18:22,136
by continuing here in America
where it all began.

1235
01:18:22,597 --> 01:18:24,838
Cheer world, here's The Truth.

1236
01:18:27,002 --> 01:18:28,310
Get ready.

1237
01:18:32,340 --> 01:18:33,944
We're about to show you up.

1238
01:18:39,247 --> 01:18:40,351
Posers.

1239
01:18:41,316 --> 01:18:43,023
Y'all a bunch of posers.

1240
01:20:17,112 --> 01:20:19,167
You gotta give it to her.
The girl is intense.

1241
01:20:19,247 --> 01:20:21,603
Yeah. She went up to a prep
with an assisted back flip

1242
01:20:21,683 --> 01:20:22,971
to an extension straight cradle

1243
01:20:23,051 --> 01:20:25,574
to a retake shoulder sit,
and a back walk out.

1244
01:20:25,654 --> 01:20:26,655
That girl is crazy.

1245
01:21:43,064 --> 01:21:46,011
That routine was pretty amazing.

1246
01:21:46,368 --> 01:21:48,211
The Truth is on fire.

1247
01:21:48,303 --> 01:21:50,592
I believe they scorched that mat.

1248
01:21:50,672 --> 01:21:52,948
Cheerpeers, watch out.

1249
01:21:53,308 --> 01:21:55,379
Jeff. Jeff.

1250
01:21:55,744 --> 01:21:56,779
What's wrong?

1251
01:21:57,479 --> 01:21:58,466
Nothing.

1252
01:21:59,781 --> 01:22:02,290
All right, look, I'm just worried about
remembering everything, you know.

1253
01:22:08,623 --> 01:22:09,829
Better?

1254
01:22:11,059 --> 01:22:13,300
No. No, now I'm worried about my breath.

1255
01:22:13,495 --> 01:22:16,271
You should be. Here.

1256
01:22:22,704 --> 01:22:24,149
Wow.

1257
01:22:26,675 --> 01:22:27,745
Thanks for the gum.

1258
01:22:28,910 --> 01:22:30,082
And hey.

1259
01:22:31,212 --> 01:22:32,384
I knew you liked me.

1260
01:22:33,048 --> 01:22:34,186
I like winning more.

1261
01:22:34,349 --> 01:22:35,726
Yeah, yeah.

1262
01:22:36,518 --> 01:22:37,839
There's a lot more to come.

1263
01:22:37,919 --> 01:22:40,490
So let's hear it for the Utah Panthers.

1264
01:22:47,696 --> 01:22:51,200
Give it up for the Blue Cranes
of South Africa.

1265
01:22:54,903 --> 01:22:56,712
The Texan Titans.

1266
01:22:58,873 --> 01:23:00,216
And the Miami Waves.

1267
01:23:36,578 --> 01:23:39,718
This global event is going down
in cheer history.

1268
01:23:39,848 --> 01:23:43,038
But now it's time for our
final performance of the night.

1269
01:23:43,118 --> 01:23:44,893
The reason we're all here.

1270
01:23:45,220 --> 01:23:47,860
Ladies, gentlemen,
cheerleaders, and wannabes,

1271
01:23:48,523 --> 01:23:51,333
I give you the team
that everyone wants to beat.

1272
01:23:53,294 --> 01:23:54,568
The Rebels.

1273
01:24:09,711 --> 01:24:11,816
Five, six, seven, eight.

1274
01:25:20,548 --> 01:25:21,549
Yo.

1275
01:25:21,683 --> 01:25:23,754
- Oh, this is so good!
- Hey!

1276
01:25:24,886 --> 01:25:27,742
Stop tripping. You know that is sick.

1277
01:25:27,822 --> 01:25:30,268
I'm just giving it up for my boys.

1278
01:27:19,901 --> 01:27:22,313
Oh. That was brilliant!

1279
01:27:22,971 --> 01:27:25,393
Rebels, tonight you have shown us

1280
01:27:25,473 --> 01:27:29,285
that not only does cheer
have spirit, but soul, too.

1281
01:27:35,350 --> 01:27:36,638
How crazy was that?

1282
01:27:36,718 --> 01:27:37,805
I know.

1283
01:27:37,885 --> 01:27:39,774
We basically just cheered
in front of the entire world.

1284
01:27:39,854 --> 01:27:42,644
Right? It makes what we've been
doing seem so small in comparison.

1285
01:27:42,724 --> 01:27:44,612
We thought we were the shit.

1286
01:27:44,692 --> 01:27:46,181
Um, we are the shit?

1287
01:27:46,261 --> 01:27:48,332
- We couldn't have done it without you.
- I know.

1288
01:27:49,264 --> 01:27:50,299
What are you doing?

1289
01:27:50,531 --> 01:27:52,787
Oh, you've just got
a little something right here.

1290
01:27:52,867 --> 01:27:54,422
Oh, I thought you were
going to try and kiss me.

1291
01:27:54,502 --> 01:27:55,981
Well, that's because I am.

1292
01:28:03,211 --> 01:28:04,365
What are you thinking about?

1293
01:28:04,445 --> 01:28:06,034
I don't know how you guys
do this all the time.

1294
01:28:06,114 --> 01:28:07,135
It's way too much pressure.

1295
01:28:07,215 --> 01:28:09,604
Now it's up to everyone watching.

1296
01:28:09,684 --> 01:28:12,373
The winner will be determined
by combining the hits

1297
01:28:12,453 --> 01:28:16,401
of each squad's video along
with the votes cast on my website.

1298
01:28:17,592 --> 01:28:20,266
I'll be back in two hours
to reveal the results.

1299
01:28:20,528 --> 01:28:21,529
Bye for now.

1300
01:28:26,801 --> 01:28:30,825
Yes, I'm so proud of my spirit children.

1301
01:28:30,905 --> 01:28:33,494
What you have done through
this Internet competition

1302
01:28:33,574 --> 01:28:35,679
has brought cheer to the masses.

1303
01:28:36,844 --> 01:28:38,266
This cheersmackdown

1304
01:28:38,346 --> 01:28:40,468
has been the biggest and most extravagant

1305
01:28:40,548 --> 01:28:42,637
cheer competition I've ever seen.

1306
01:28:42,717 --> 01:28:44,739
Regardless of who wins,

1307
01:28:44,819 --> 01:28:48,028
tonight's event will forever
go down in spirit history.

1308
01:28:48,790 --> 01:28:51,600
All right. It's time.

1309
01:28:52,026 --> 01:28:56,184
Cheer teams, get ready for the results.

1310
01:29:00,702 --> 01:29:04,292
I'm sure that some of the teams
that you've watched tonight

1311
01:29:04,372 --> 01:29:07,717
will be making history at the Olympic Games.

1312
01:29:12,647 --> 01:29:16,337
As we all know, the winner
will be determined by the hits,

1313
01:29:16,417 --> 01:29:18,658
plus the votes cast on my website.

1314
01:29:19,053 --> 01:29:21,276
And I will give you that final decision now.

1315
01:29:21,356 --> 01:29:22,410
I can't take it.

1316
01:29:22,490 --> 01:29:23,491
Me either.

1317
01:29:33,968 --> 01:29:37,575
The winner of the first ever
cheersmackdown is...

1318
01:29:47,482 --> 01:29:48,483
The Rebels.

1319
01:30:06,100 --> 01:30:08,444
- Whoo!
- What are you doing? We lost.

1320
01:30:08,536 --> 01:30:11,415
I know. But our friends won.

1321
01:30:11,706 --> 01:30:13,413
Oh. Right.

